# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Twilight Forest — Fabric access widener (ported from META-INF/accesstransformer.cfg)
#
# The Forge branch used an access transformer with SRG names (f_xxxxx_, m_xxxxx_).
# This widener uses OFFICIAL MOJANG (named) names — required because the project
# compiles against loom.officialMojangMappings().
#
# CONVERSION NOTES
#  * Class names are NOT obfuscated, so AT method/field *descriptors* are already
#    mojmap-valid and were copied verbatim (just `.`→`/`).
#  * The AT comments (e.g. "# skyBuffer") gave the mojmap member name — those are
#    pre-filled below so migration is fill-in-descriptor, not rediscovery.
#  * Forge AT → widener mapping:
#       public  CLASS            -> accessible class
#       public  field            -> accessible field
#       public-f field           -> accessible field + mutable field
#       public/protected method  -> accessible method   (+ extendable method if overridden)
#  * Loom FAILS the build if a widener entry targets a member that does not exist
#    in 1.20.1. Several 1.19.2 entries are GONE in 1.20.1 (flagged ⚠ REMOVED/CHANGED
#    below) and MUST stay disabled until the using code is rewritten.
#
# STRATEGY: entries are activated incrementally as each using class is ported and
# its compile error appears. Only version-stable, descriptor-complete entries are
# active now; the rest are staged as comments with everything pre-resolved.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

